 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** The method requires two convolutions per sample, but they are performed simultaneously using SIMD instructions, avoiding the bottleneck of computing two different expensive filters [S1]. The prefiltering step is performed once per volume, adding a one-time cost [S1].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Not given in the sources. [S1]
-*   **Performance:** The technique enables efficient GPU implementation via SIMD instructions [S1].
-*   **Strengths:** The method provides interactive control over the trade-off between smoothing and postaliasing effects on the fly [S1]. It offers a continuous transition between approximating and prefiltered interpolating reconstructions [S1].
-*   **Limitations:** The choice of an appropriate filter depends on the data set and the specific visualization task, so a universal solution does not exist [S1].
-*   **When to Use:** Not given in the sources. [S1]
-*   **When Not to Use:** Not given in the sources. [S1]
